<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalanikūpule</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1760–<a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Kalanikupule</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalanikūpule was the last independent ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oʻahu</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahekili-ii">Kahekili II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maui">Maui</a>. On his father's death in 1794 he defeated and killed his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaeokulani">Kaʻeokulani</a> with the help of the British trader William Brown, then tried to seize Brown's ships, killing him. In 1795 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i">Kamehameha I</a> invaded Oʻahu and defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nuuanu">Battle of Nuʻuanu</a>; he fled into the hills but was captured and sacrificed.</p></div>
